      shortDescription: "Attention lets a model compute weighted interactions between representations so it can focus on relevant information when producing an output",
      explanation: "Fundamental questions expose gaps in first principles and show how clearly the candidate reasons about machine learning.",
      sampleAnswer: "Attention lets a model compute weighted interactions between representations so it can focus on relevant information when producing an output. In self-attention, each token can use information from other tokens in the sequence. This helps models represent long-range relationships more directly than sequential recurrence.",
      detailedAnswer: "Attention is a mechanism that allows a neural network to dynamically focus on the most relevant parts of an input when producing a representation or prediction.\n\nInstead of treating every input element as equally important, attention calculates weights indicating how strongly different elements should contribute to the current representation.\n\nA simplified attention process is:\n\n```text\nQuery + Keys -> attention scores\nattention scores -> normalized weights\nweights + Values -> weighted representation\n```\n\nFor example, in a sentence such as:\n\n```text\n'The animal didn't cross the road because it was tired.'\n```\n\nWhen interpreting the word 'it', attention can assign stronger weight to relevant earlier words such as 'animal' rather than treating all words equally.\n\nThe most common formulation in transformers uses Query, Key, and Value matrices. Scaled dot-product attention can be represented as:\n\n```text\nAttention(Q, K, V) = softmax(QK? / sqrt(d?))V\n```\n\nThe scaling factor helps keep the dot products at a numerically useful scale before the softmax operation.\n\nSelf-attention means the queries, keys, and values come from the same sequence. This allows each token to directly incorporate information from other tokens in the sequence.\n\nAttention is powerful because it can model relationships between distant elements without requiring information to pass through a long recurrent chain.\n\nHowever, standard full self-attention has computational and memory costs that grow roughly quadratically with sequence length, which becomes important for very long contexts.\n\nInterview takeaway: attention lets a model assign different weights to different input elements so that it can focus on the information most relevant to the current representation or prediction.",
      keyPoints: ["Whether the candidate can explain the core machine-learning concept accurately and relate it to a practical modeling decision.\\n\\n"],
      commonMistakes: [],
      followUpQuestions: ["What is the purpose of a train/validation/test split?", "How would you compare two models fairly?", "How would you decide whether a more complex model is worth using?"],
      tags: ["machine-learning", "attention"],
      seoTitle: "What is attention? | Machine Learning Interview Question",
      seoDescription: "Attention lets a model compute weighted interactions between representations so it can focus on relevant information when producing an output",
      isPublished: true,
